node_modules

# Secrets.
# `.env` alone was not enough: an `.env.bak.<timestamp>` created while editing
# config was left tracked, and would have published every credential in the file
# to the remote. Glob every variant and re-include only the template.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Uploaded documents and media.
# These are user data, not source. Committing them bloats the repo and puts
# private files (medical certificates, ID documents, chat attachments) into git
# history, where deleting them later does not remove them.
# Production stores these under UPLOAD_ROOT, outside the repo entirely.
uploads/
